      <string id="LanguageTone">Language tone of new recordings</string>
      <string id="LanguageTone_Help">How the steps of new recordings are worded. Casual is Steps' own short style ("Click "Save""); Plain language uses everyday words ("Select the "Save" button"); Formal writes full sentences ("Click the "Save" button."). Staff can't change it in Settings while this is set; a guide can still be reworded with Language and tone.

Not configured: casual, and each person can choose another in Settings > Recording.</string>
      <string id="ShowUnnamedTyping">Show typing into unnamed boxes</string>
      <string id="ShowUnnamedTyping_Help">Whether a step shows what was typed into something the recording couldn't name, such as a document or a box with no label. Enabled: shown, as for named fields. Disabled: the step says only "Type", and the person can show the text step by step. Staff can't change it in Settings while this is set.

Not configured: off, and each person can turn it on in Settings > Recording.</string>
      <string id="BlurStrength">Blur suggestions</string>
      <string id="BlurStrength_Help">How much Steps looks for in screenshots to suggest blurring. Light: emails, phone, card and bank numbers, and the always-blur words. Standard: also postcodes, National Insurance numbers, names and IDs beside their labels, and the person's own Windows and OneDrive account names. Thorough: also file names (such as recent-file lists) and file paths. Suggestions are never blurred by themselves: people blur them, one at a time or all at once. Staff can't change it in Settings while this is set.

Not configured: standard, and each person can choose another in Settings > Privacy.</string>
      <string id="Blur_light">Light</string>
      <string id="Blur_standard">Standard</string>
      <string id="Blur_thorough">Thorough</string>
      <string id="Tone_casual">Casual</string>
      <string id="Tone_plain">Plain language</string>
      <string id="Tone_formal">Formal</string>
    </stringTable>
    <presentationTable>
      <presentation id="Libraries">
        <multiTextBox refId="Libraries">Libraries (one per line, Name=Path):</multiTextBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="DefaultLibrary">
        <textBox refId="DefaultLibrary">
          <label>Library name or folder:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="ExcludedApps">
        <multiTextBox refId="ExcludedApps">Program file names (one per line):</multiTextBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="Locked">
        <multiTextBox refId="Locked">Settings to lock (one per line):</multiTextBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="BlurTerms">
        <multiTextBox refId="BlurTerms">Words and phrases (one per line):</multiTextBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="SensitiveFieldPatterns">
        <multiTextBox refId="SensitiveFieldPatterns">Field name words (one per line):</multiTextBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="BrandProfiles">
        <multiTextBox refId="BrandProfiles">Brand files (one full path per line):</multiTextBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="AppColoursBrand">
        <textBox refId="AppColoursBrand">
          <label>Brand profile id:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="DefaultPdfBrand">
        <textBox refId="DefaultPdfBrand">
          <label>Brand profile id:</label>
        </textBox>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="Language">
        <dropdownList refId="Language" defaultItem="0">Language:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="LanguageTone">
        <dropdownList refId="LanguageTone" defaultItem="0">Language tone:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
      <presentation id="BlurStrength">
        <dropdownList refId="BlurStrength" defaultItem="1">Blur suggestions:</dropdownList>
      </presentation>
    </presentationTable>
  </resources>
</policyDefinitionResources>
